I had been amazed by director Antal's Kontroll back in 2003. So what can I say about it? It's a fantastic film! But this has its peculiarities as well, such as:

• it takes a long time to film. I'm not even sure they had to reshoot (a movie of this sort usually does that);

• it does not take place in a normal world. There was a brief scene right before the scene where Jules is about to make love with the woman;

• the audience is never told what happened to Pina. The whole movie is an exercise in making up nonsense. The movie seems to be so concerned with its own fictional world that Jules doesn't even know exactly why he was involved in the disaster;

• a lot of the people in the movie have "death" in their names, some of them seem to be just zombies, and even the person who talks to Pina is called "D.D."! (This is not a movie I want to hear my name pronounced! I just want you to get it straight before you ask me an annoying question that will drive me to tears!);

• the scene when Jules makes love to Pina is pretty cheesy. I don't even know how I feel about that scene anymore.

The story seems to consist of two scenes. (I'm not allowed to give details, so I'll describe them with the bare minimum of details.) At the end of the first one the person who had been a zombie is actually revealed to be Jules. At the beginning of the second scene the guy who was wearing the glasses and talking to Jules is revealed to be Pina.

After the two scenes I was really confused and could not understand what the point of the movie was. It just goes on and on.

